task: Create a Spring Boot service named calculator-service from scratch: a REST API for a basic calculator. GET /api/v1/calculator/{operation}?a=<number>&b=<number> returns JSON {"result": <number>}. Operations: add, subtract, multiply, divide, power (a to the power of b), sqrt (square root of a, b is not used). Division by zero, the square root of a negative number, an unknown operation or a missing parameter return 400. Use Java 25, the latest Spring Boot 3.5.x and Gradle Kotlin DSL. The Gradle wrapper is already in the project.
